      <h3>Information We Collect</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>User Provided Information:</strong> You provide certain personally identifiable information (such as your name, email address, username, and profile photo) to SportsBeep when registering for an account, participating in contests, or using other features of the Service. You may also optionally provide your <strong>Cardano blockchain wallet address</strong> for $BEEP token transactions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Blockchain Information:</strong> If you provide a Cardano wallet address, we may access publicly available blockchain data associated with that address, including transaction history and token balances. Blockchain data is inherently public and transparent.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cookies Information:</strong> When you visit SportsBeep.com, we may send one or more cookies to your computer or device to uniquely identify your browser. We use both session cookies and persistent cookies. You may reset your browser to refuse cookies, but some features may not function properly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Log File Information:</strong> Our servers may automatically record information including your web request, IP address, browser type, referring/exit pages, platform type, pages viewed, and the date and time of your request.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Mobile App Information:</strong> When you use our mobile app, we may collect device information such as operating system, hardware type, device identifiers, device state, language, location, and app usage data.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h3>How We Use Your Information</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>To operate, maintain, and provide the features and functionality of SportsBeep, including contest management, scoring, and $BEEP token distribution</li>
        <li>To process contest entries, calculate scores, and distribute winnings</li>
        <li>To facilitate blockchain transactions and $BEEP token transfers to your Cardano wallet</li>
        <li>To contact you for marketing and administrative purposes (such as contest results or account updates)</li>
        <li>To improve the quality and design of SportsBeep and create new features</li>
        <li>To monitor aggregate metrics such as total visitors, pages viewed, and contest participation</li>
        <li>We may anonymize or aggregate your information for business purposes, including reporting and research</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>When We Disclose Information</h3>
      <p>Our subsidiaries, affiliated companies, or authorized partners may access your information for processing purposes. We may share personally identifiable information with third parties for marketing with your consent. We will publish your username, membership date, and contest statistics on your profile page.</p>
      <p>SportsBeep reserves the right to disclose personally identifiable information that we believe is appropriate or necessary to enforce our Terms of Service, protect our rights, respond to legal requests, or protect safety.</p>
      <p><strong>Blockchain Transparency:</strong> Please note that transactions on the Cardano blockchain are publicly visible. While we do not publicly link your account to your wallet address, blockchain transactions themselves are transparent and traceable.</p>

      <h3>Your Choices</h3>
      <p>You may decline to submit personally identifiable information, in which case SportsBeep may not be able to provide certain services. You may also choose not to link a Cardano wallet address, though this will limit your ability to receive $BEEP token rewards.</p>
      <p>To protect your privacy and security, we take reasonable steps to verify your identity before granting profile access or making corrections.</p>

      <h3>Data Security</h3>
      <p>SportsBeep uses commercially reasonable physical, managerial, and technical safeguards to preserve the integrity and security of your personal information. However, we cannot guarantee absolute security of information transmitted to SportsBeep.</p>

      <h3>Merger, Sale, or Bankruptcy</h3>
      <p>In the event that SportsBeep is involved in a merger, acquisition, sale, bankruptcy, or other change of control, your personally identifiable information may be disclosed to another entity related to such event.</p>

      <h3>Third Party Advertising</h3>
      <p>Certain ads appearing on SportsBeep may be delivered by advertising partners who may use cookies and automated technologies to collect data. To learn more and opt out, visit <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info/choices</a>.</p>

      <h3>Publicity</h3>
      <p>Participation in a contest constitutes the player's consent to the use by SportsBeep of the player's name, likeness, and biographical information for promotional purposes, as described in our <a href="/tos">Terms of Service</a>.</p>

      <h3>Your California Privacy Rights</h3>
      <p>If you reside in California, you may request information regarding our disclosure of personal information to third parties for their direct marketing purposes. Contact us at the address listed above.</p>

